  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajendra Prasasd Dubey vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 27 February, 2024 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia 1 Mcrc No.45503/2022 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia On The 27th Of February, 2024 Misc. Criminal Case No. 45503 of 2022 Between:- 1. Rajendra Prasasd Dubey S/O Shri Radhika Prasad Dubey, Aged About 68 Years, Occupation: Agriculture R/O Village Domhai, Sabhapur, Bisirsinghpur, District Satna (Madhya Pradesh) 2. SHIVKANTI DUBEY W/O SHRI RAJENDRA PRASAD DUBEY, AGED ABOUT 65 YEARS, OCCUPATION: HOUSE WIFE R/O VILLAGE DOMHAI, SABHAPUR, BISIRSINGHPUR, DISTRICT SATNA (MADHYA PRADESH) 3. DEEPAK DUBEY S/O SHRI RAJENDRA PRASAD DUBEY, AGED ABOUT 28 YEARS, OCCUPATION: STUDENT R/O VILLAGE DOMHAI, SABHAPUR, BISIRSINGHPUR, DISTRICT SATNA (MADHYA PRADESH) .....APPLICANTS (BY SHRI SWAPNIL SOHGAURA - ADVOCATE) AND 1. STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH POLICE STATION MAIHAR DISTRICT SATNA (MADHYA PRADESH) 2. PRABHA DUBEY D/O LATE SHRI HETLAL PANDEY, AGED ABOUT 32 YEARS, R/O VILLAGE AMDA, TEHSIL MAIHAR, DISTRICT SATNA (MADHYA PRADESH) Rajendra Prasasd Dubey vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 27 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/85013123/ 1 .....RESPONDENTS (BY SHRI K.S. BAGHEL - GOVERNMENT ADVOCATE FOR RESPONDENT NO.1/STATE) 2 MCRC No.45503/2022 This application coming on for admission this day, the court passed the following: ORDER",
    "facts": "Whenever, the complainant insisted that she wants to reside with her husband, then her father-in-law, mother-in-law as well as husband used to abuse and used to pass taunts that the parents of the complainant have not given the dowry as per the status of their family and therefore, her husband cannot not take her back to Mumbai. Even abusive language was being used.",
    "arguments": "The only stand taken by applicants is that FIR has been lodged after the filing of divorce petition. On the contrary, that shows that the lady tried her level best to save her married life and only when she realized that there is no possibility of improvement, then she lodged the FIR."
  },
