    ],
    "annotations_dropped": [
      {
        "annotation_id": "a19afb8d414142288ddb25dd0b4a83f6_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bquashed\\b",
            "matched_text": "quashed",
            "start": 127,
            "end": 134
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "8. The Supreme Court in the case of Pratibha v. Rameshwari Devi, reported in (2007) 12 SCC 369 has held that the FIR cannot be quashed only on the ground that it was lodged after the divorce petition was filed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7456de507365494a9888e54fd6b62a11_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nFurthermore, the judgment passed in the Civil Court is not binding on the criminal Court and the filing of the divorce petition cannot be a ground to quash the FIR."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0f1a55c233e349e39c241830830ccd8c_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. So far as allegations made against the applicants are concerned, it is the case of respondent No.2 that since her husband was posted in Mumbai, therefore, she was residing in her matrimonial house alongwith her father-in-law, mother-in-l"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "08eae376e0b84f56b2b4f11bb5a7d2d2_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are specific allegations against applicants Nos.1 and 2 that they were passing taunts to the effect that parents of complainant has not given the dowry as per the status of their family."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "48c4903a99b841fdac3f0cc55ea1662f_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nRajendra Prasasd Dubey vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 27 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/85013123/\n3 10."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "209789e8d704469d9335a5a4a99ad560_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "So far as applicant No.3, who is the younger brother-in-law of complainant is concerned, there are specific allegations that he also used the word panoti and other filthy languages and was in habit of insulting her and was all the time sayi"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9d8fadfaf4bc4fb7abc3e9cee5f7bda1_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are further allegations that mother-in-law and younger brother-in- law were not providing financial help to bear day to day expenses and they were always saying that it is not their duty to look after her."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4d4f130a9aa6457fa925a0046a9d9ed9_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Father- in-law and mother-in-law also used to threat her that in case if anything is narrated by her to anybody then she would be killed and when respondent No.2 was called by some unknown lady from Mumbai who informed that Ajay Dubey is he"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "21f542dfdd6a434580dcc8a5a4453de3_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is true that in the light of judgments by Supreme Court in the case of Kans Raj v. State of Punjab, reported in (2000) 5 SCC 207, Monju Roy v. State of W.B., reported in (2015) 13 SCC 693 and Chandralekha & Ors. v. State of Rajasthan & A"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "45022fdb1f9c40ffbeae8e7623e67294_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However if the facts of the present case are considered, then it is clear that applicant No.3, who is the younger brother-in-law of respondent No.2 used to call her by word panoti and also used to scold her that after her marriage developme"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1b28fdea9e344634a32001a4f1568c6c_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even financial help was not being provided to her to bear the day to day expenses."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "492851beb451442192f2b751ce9dba0a_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Use of word panoti with an intention to cause annoyance to Bhabhi may come under the purview of cruelty as defined under Section 498-A of IPC because humiliation of a person by calling her as panoti will certainly would be willful conduct w"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "acebd1b15d2941f5b011028dbc67f61b_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. So far as applicants Nos.1 and 2 are concerned, there are specific allegations that they used to pass taunts against respondent No.2 on account of less dowry brought by her."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "223349d08e79469e91c5722bdf7b9a2e_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They used to abuse respondent No.2."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2c500fcbd6d94e719ced421addbbdc19_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They also used to threat her that in case if anything is narrated by her to anybody,\nthen she and her brother would be killed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ec84430f49994fe6b5d009b7bbefec60_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "When she suffered heart attack as well as mental shock,\nthen all the expenses of treatment were borne by brother of respondent No.2.\n13."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b41a38dc578e4f65a4789261c6be9872_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Supreme Court in the case of Taramani Parakh Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh and Others reported in (2015) 11 SCC 260 has held as under:-\n\"12."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c66c91dc097c44488e2f7436a31890e1_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kailash Chandra Agrawal v. State of U.P. [Kailash Chandra Agrawal v. State of U.P., (2014) 16 SCC 551], it was observed (SCC p. 553, paras 8-9):\n\"8."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d5a09acf7f774584ab47b61e99be241d_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We have gone through the FIR and the criminal complaint."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b33f2e088da44fff91fbd0bb65419b41_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the FIR, the appellants have not been named and in the criminal complaint they have been named without attributing any specific role to them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a1a253c74f984a8c8df55c5c2b75729c_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The relationship of the appellants with the husband of the complainant is distant."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a30b584bcc4f48de990f20d480010075_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kans Raj v. State of Punjab [Kans Raj v.\nState of Punjab, (2000) 5 SCC 207 : 2000 SCC (Cri) 935 : (2000) 3 SCR 662"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a66a5ff9df454594af69e5939c28fd5d_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "] it was observed (SCC p. 217, para 5):\n\"5. ... A tendency has, however, developed for roping in all relations of the in-laws of the deceased wives in the matters of dowry deaths which, if not discouraged, is likely Rajendra Prasasd Dubey v"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ec212f7abc75480aaa50fa79a475a370_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In their overenthusiasm and anxiety to seek conviction for maximum people, the parents of the deceased have been found to be making efforts for involving other relations which ultimately weaken the case of the prosecution even against the r"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a9e4f5e88de1431a9a52643f1464393b_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe Court has, thus, to be careful in summoning distant relatives without there being specific material."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5440f2af42744245aa981d66f6b4ee40_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Only the husband, his parents or at best close family members may be expected to demand dowry or to harass the wife but not distant relations, unless there is tangible material to support allegations made against such distant relations."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e3b6b60b3ea5433e985d314e54a4c0c5_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Mere naming of distant relations is not enough to summon them in the absence of any specific role and material to support such role."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5497a6fb5d364018a46c2707e08a9866_68",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n9. The parameters for quashing proceedings in a criminal complaint are well known."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "03fd656a701b4781ad0cea11c6554e1a_69",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If there are triable issues, the Court is not expected to go into the veracity of the rival versions but where on the face of it, the criminal proceedings are abuse of Court's process, quashing jurisdiction can be exercised."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a39dadb67a364be480b89e04c3f97849_70",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference may be made to K. Ramakrishna v. State of Bihar [K. Ramakrishna v. State of Bihar, (2000) 8 SCC 547 : 2001 SCC (Cri) 27] , Pepsi Foods Ltd. v. Judicial Magistrate [Pepsi Foods Ltd. v. Judicial Magistrate, (1998) 5 SCC 749 : 1998 S"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2bad830a396c4bccbe5c17e36050cd1b_71",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, the complaint is as follows:\n\"Sir, it is submitted that I was married on 18-11-2009 with Sidharath Parakh s/o Manak Chand Parakh r/o Sarafa Bazar in front of Radha Krishna Market, Gwalior according to the Hindu rites an"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "86572316971741bd9100c3675153ce1f_72",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the marriage my father had given gold and silver ornaments, cash amount and household goods according to his capacity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b199730df6e6432c981b5fe360b510b3_73",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nAfter the marriage when I went to my matrimonial home, I was treated nicely by the members of the family."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a07bb73de9c94f2c8ed78a664fbedf56_74",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "When on the second occasion I went to my matrimonial home, my husband, father-in-law and mother-in-law started harassing me for not bringing the dowry and started saying that I should bring from my father 25-30 tolas of gold and Rs 2,00,000"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9a7fdf4324254776813ddccd78e6c38e_75",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On account of this my husband also used to beat me and my father-in-law and my mother-in-law used to torture me by giving the taunts."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6784f6ebe8864d75b6ad5aadda11cd5a_76",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In this connection I used to tell my father Kundanmal Oswal, my mother Smt Prem Lata Oswal, uncle Ashok Rai Sharma and uncle Ved Prakash Mishra from time to time."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "67fcc784a8bb482e9d7bae523629e494_77",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On 2-4-2010 the members of the family of my matrimonial home forcibly sent me to the house of my parents in Ganj Basoda along with my brother Deepak."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5177acd1ee6748479a0f24bf7da24c89_78",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They snatched my clothes and ornaments and kept with them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6ff633c2aab64187b00fbe3cd4c5c67f_79",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Since then till today my husband has been harassing me on the telephone and has not come to take me back."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b1e98b4aa3d74221a011884f5d5656b3_80",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Being compelled, I have been moving this application before you."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d6340fc460824339badff2546f5f8e2a_81",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sir, it is prayed that action be taken against husband Sidharath Parakh, my father-in-law Manak Chand Parakh and my mother-in-law Smt Indira Parakh for torturing me on account of Rajendra Prasasd Dubey vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 27 F"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9d9f41278cd7452f9011fcc2683e8fb4_82",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. From a reading of the complaint, it cannot be held that even if the allegations are taken as proved no case is made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7166214767024f7294a26467322e579a_83",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are allegations against Respondent 2 and his parents for harassing the complainant which forced her to leave the matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "08a758445bed4629b77f7f1f41e853f0_84",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even now she continues to be separated from the matrimonial home as she apprehends lack of security and safety and proper environment in the matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ff221cc9a8d54f9d98b64a37f9b2fcc1_85",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
